  body+=section('One chapter. One connected story.','''<p>The central question is <strong>“What can we make by adding vectors and multiplying them by numbers?”</strong> Equations ask for the right coefficients. Independence asks whether those coefficients are unique. A basis gives every vector an address. A linear map moves the vectors, while a basis change only changes their addresses.</p><div class="route"><span>Constraints</span><b>→</b><span>Combinations</span><b>→</b><span>Spaces & bases</span><b>→</b><span>Maps & coordinates</span></div>''')
