  body+=section('About this companion','''<p>Based on a reading of all of Chapter 2 (printed pp. 17–69, including Exercises 2.1–2.20) in your local <em>Mathematics for Machine Learning</em> PDF by Marc Peter Deisenroth, A. Aldo Faisal, and Cheng Soon Ong, draft dated January 15, 2024. The explanations and diagrams are written for this companion; selected small examples are identified where they follow the book.</p><p>PDF page numbers are six higher than printed numbers in this file, so printed p. 17 is PDF page 23. Every lesson links to its starting page. All diagrams, typography, and interactions work offline, with no external libraries. Progress is stored in this browser when local storage is available; some browsers restrict persistence for local files. The lessons and expandable explanations remain readable without JavaScript.</p><p>The illustrations use ordinary 2D coordinates for intuition. Lengths and angles are not the focus until Chapter 3. The practice guide includes hints and selected results, rather than a complete solutions manual.</p>''')
